WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.142
Previously.

00:00:01.142 --> 00:00:04.670
On Sidefighter: The Week That Changed Everything.

00:00:05.820 --> 00:00:07.120
Six fighters.

00:00:07.120 --> 00:00:08.420
One fireball.

00:00:08.420 --> 00:00:09.520
No regrets.

00:00:09.520 --> 00:00:12.420
And one review, from one man.

00:00:13.770 --> 00:00:15.450
Kinda janky, he said.

00:00:15.450 --> 00:00:17.690
Basically, Mortal Kombat it.

00:00:20.040 --> 00:00:21.198
That man was Tony.

00:00:21.198 --> 00:00:22.999
This film is not about Tony.

00:00:22.999 --> 00:00:25.122
Tony would want you to know that.

00:00:25.122 --> 00:00:28.210
Tony would also want you to know about the jank.

00:00:30.360 --> 00:00:31.182
In the beginning...

00:00:31.182 --> 00:00:31.960
there was nothing.

00:00:34.510 --> 00:00:39.439
Just twelve thousand, one hundred and two three-dimensional models.

00:00:39.439 --> 00:00:40.101
Sleeping.

00:00:40.101 --> 00:00:40.910
In folders.

00:00:42.460 --> 00:00:44.549
Soldiers who had never walked.

00:00:44.549 --> 00:00:46.917
Tanks that had never fired a shot.

00:00:46.917 --> 00:00:50.190
Trees that had never cast a shadow on anything.

00:00:51.940 --> 00:00:54.745
This is the story of what happened next.

00:00:54.745 --> 00:00:56.007
It took four days.

00:00:56.007 --> 00:00:57.690
Tony would say it shows.

00:01:10.740 --> 00:01:13.256
Thursday, the fifteenth of October.

00:01:13.256 --> 00:01:16.060
Twenty-nine minutes past ten, at night.

00:01:17.310 --> 00:01:22.442
While the rest of the world was asleep, one commit landed.

00:01:22.442 --> 00:01:23.061
Ingest.

00:01:23.061 --> 00:01:23.769
Library.

00:01:23.769 --> 00:01:24.831
Retargeting.

00:01:24.831 --> 00:01:25.450
Studio.

00:01:26.700 --> 00:01:29.336
Eight minutes later: view standards.

00:01:29.336 --> 00:01:33.070
Projections, direction sets, mirroring, scale lock.

00:01:34.320 --> 00:01:38.893
Fifteen minutes after that: export formats for every engine that mattered.

00:01:38.893 --> 00:01:41.427
Most companies would call that a quarter.

00:01:41.427 --> 00:01:42.910
We called it a Thursday.

00:01:48.360 --> 00:01:51.578
Here is the problem every game developer knows.

00:01:51.578 --> 00:01:53.358
You have beautiful 3D art.

00:01:53.358 --> 00:01:54.727
You need 2D sprites.

00:01:54.727 --> 00:01:56.233
And between the two...

00:01:56.233 --> 00:01:57.260
lies suffering.

00:01:58.510 --> 00:02:01.050
The Synty Sprite Generator ends the suffering.

00:02:02.600 --> 00:02:03.851
Eight directions.

00:02:03.851 --> 00:02:04.587
Isometric.

00:02:04.587 --> 00:02:12.165
Real scale, locked to the tile, so a soldier is the size of a soldier and a tank is the size of a tank.

00:02:12.165 --> 00:02:13.636
That sounds obvious.

00:02:13.636 --> 00:02:14.740
Nobody does it.

00:02:15.990 --> 00:02:17.666
Objects have states.

00:02:17.666 --> 00:02:19.257
A bunker is intact.

00:02:19.257 --> 00:02:20.849
Then it is damaged.

00:02:20.849 --> 00:02:24.200
Then it is a smoking hole in the ground.

00:02:24.200 --> 00:02:25.122
One sprite.

00:02:25.122 --> 00:02:26.127
Every state.

00:02:26.127 --> 00:02:27.970
Every collision shape.

00:02:34.120 --> 00:02:35.561
We built a game.

00:02:35.561 --> 00:02:36.552
A real one.

00:02:36.552 --> 00:02:37.994
Solitary Strike.

00:02:37.994 --> 00:02:40.876
One soldier, behind enemy lines.

00:02:42.126 --> 00:02:44.653
And we gave the game one rule.

00:02:44.653 --> 00:02:47.095
You may not touch the engine.

00:02:47.095 --> 00:02:48.779
You may only ask it.

00:02:48.779 --> 00:02:49.874
Command line.

00:02:49.874 --> 00:02:50.211
MCP.

00:02:50.211 --> 00:02:51.306
Nothing else.

00:02:52.556 --> 00:02:58.338
Every time the game needed something the engine couldn't do, it wrote it down.

00:02:58.338 --> 00:02:59.598
A feedback entry.

00:02:59.598 --> 00:03:00.265
Numbered.

00:03:00.265 --> 00:03:00.710
Dated.

00:03:00.710 --> 00:03:01.896
Brutally honest.

00:03:03.146 --> 00:03:04.756
Ninety-nine of them.

00:03:04.756 --> 00:03:06.848
The engine read every one.

00:03:06.848 --> 00:03:07.975
It fixed them.

00:03:07.975 --> 00:03:13.046
The game came back, deleted its workaround, and wrote one word.

00:03:13.046 --> 00:03:13.770
Verified.

00:03:13.770 --> 00:03:16.346
Sixty-seven times, and counting.

00:03:18.496 --> 00:03:20.591
And some were found by Tony.

00:03:20.591 --> 00:03:21.788
Tony has a gift.

00:03:21.788 --> 00:03:28.446
He looks at the thing everyone else has stared at for six hours, and he says the obvious.

00:03:28.446 --> 00:03:29.120
Out loud.

00:03:29.120 --> 00:03:29.943
Every time.

00:03:29.943 --> 00:03:31.364
He is always right.

00:03:31.364 --> 00:03:32.636
It is unbearable.

00:03:38.986 --> 00:03:41.225
How do you build this much, this fast?

00:03:41.225 --> 00:03:43.346
You don't do it one thing at a time.

00:03:44.596 --> 00:03:45.509
Twelve waves.

00:03:45.509 --> 00:03:48.178
Three hundred and thirty-four commits.

00:03:48.178 --> 00:03:50.637
Eighty-five thousand lines of code.

00:03:50.637 --> 00:03:51.550
In four days.

00:03:51.550 --> 00:03:56.186
Andrew estimates it is only a few million commits away from ready.

00:04:02.536 --> 00:04:03.070
And this...

00:04:03.070 --> 00:04:03.896
is what it built.

00:04:05.246 --> 00:04:06.057
One commando.

00:04:06.057 --> 00:04:12.419
Dropped behind enemy lines, with three supply pods and a clock that does not care about your feelings.

00:04:13.669 --> 00:04:15.223
Machine-gun nests.

00:04:15.223 --> 00:04:16.778
Hidden minefields.

00:04:16.778 --> 00:04:17.555
Trenches.

00:04:17.555 --> 00:04:21.959
Tanks, that only a rocket or a time bomb will stop.

00:04:23.209 --> 00:04:24.340
Blow the depot.

00:04:24.340 --> 00:04:25.849
Steal the code book.

00:04:25.849 --> 00:04:30.677
Capture the officer, and he surrenders, and he follows you home.

00:04:30.677 --> 00:04:32.110
Free the prisoners.

00:04:32.110 --> 00:04:34.599
Photograph the prototype, unseen.

00:04:35.849 --> 00:04:37.349
Then call the plane.

00:04:37.349 --> 00:04:38.249
And hold on.

00:04:40.399 --> 00:04:44.296
Today, Solitary Strike is played all over the world.

00:04:44.296 --> 00:04:44.895
By Tony.

00:04:52.045 --> 00:04:54.371
Monday, the nineteenth of October.

00:04:54.371 --> 00:04:55.876
Seventeen forty-seven.

00:04:55.876 --> 00:04:58.475
The first playtester enters the field.

00:04:59.825 --> 00:05:01.194
His first finding.

00:05:01.194 --> 00:05:03.627
An enemy soldier, incapacitated.

00:05:03.627 --> 00:05:07.125
In his words, overwhelmed by holding that gun.

00:05:07.125 --> 00:05:09.635
And somehow, impossible to shoot.

00:05:11.185 --> 00:05:13.910
Undeterred, he destroys a tank.

00:05:13.910 --> 00:05:15.493
With a LAW rocket.

00:05:15.493 --> 00:05:17.251
Exactly as designed.

00:05:17.251 --> 00:05:19.625
History will remember this.

00:05:21.375 --> 00:05:22.851
He clears the stage.

00:05:22.851 --> 00:05:25.138
He reaches the extraction zone.

00:05:25.138 --> 00:05:26.835
He waits for the plane.

00:05:28.785 --> 00:05:29.584
And he waits.

00:05:29.584 --> 00:05:35.175
Standing, and I quote, with his dick in his hand, waiting for a plane that is never coming.

00:05:38.125 --> 00:05:39.386
There was a key.

00:05:39.386 --> 00:05:39.543
C.

00:05:39.543 --> 00:05:40.725
Call the plane.

00:05:40.725 --> 00:05:42.932
It had been there all along.

00:05:42.932 --> 00:05:45.138
He found it in a screenshot.

00:05:45.138 --> 00:05:46.005
Afterwards.

00:05:47.755 --> 00:05:50.187
His final report was two words long.

00:05:50.187 --> 00:05:50.795
The fuck.

00:05:53.945 --> 00:05:59.911
Less than three hours later, wave twelve put it on the screen, in plain English.

00:05:59.911 --> 00:06:00.433
Then C.

00:06:00.433 --> 00:06:01.551
Call the plane.

00:06:01.551 --> 00:06:02.744
Thank you, Tony.

00:06:02.744 --> 00:06:05.205
Head of Pointing Out the Obvious.

00:06:11.755 --> 00:06:13.930
You may have seen the first film.

00:06:13.930 --> 00:06:14.721
Sidefighter.

00:06:14.721 --> 00:06:20.455
Two mercenaries, a fireball, and a man named Ryker, who did not become a better person.

00:06:21.705 --> 00:06:24.551
Ryker is still not a better person.

00:06:24.551 --> 00:06:25.527
Same engine.

00:06:25.527 --> 00:06:26.341
Same rule.

00:06:26.341 --> 00:06:28.455
Completely different game.

00:06:30.805 --> 00:06:32.795
Four days ago, there was nothing.

00:06:35.145 --> 00:06:41.039
Today there are twelve thousand models that can walk, run, fight, burn and fall.

00:06:41.039 --> 00:06:43.102
A hundred and fifty sprites.

00:06:43.102 --> 00:06:44.207
Seventeen maps.

00:06:44.207 --> 00:06:44.944
Two games.

00:06:44.944 --> 00:06:49.365
And one engine that makes the next one easier than the last.

00:06:51.315 --> 00:06:51.569
Oh.

00:06:51.569 --> 00:06:53.175
And one more thing.

00:06:55.725 --> 00:06:56.390
This film.

00:06:56.390 --> 00:06:58.451
The shots, the music, the edit.

00:06:58.451 --> 00:07:00.845
The voice you are hearing right now.

00:07:00.845 --> 00:07:04.835
Made on the same machine, by the same process, this evening.

00:07:06.585 --> 00:07:08.664
We didn't just build a sprite engine.

00:07:08.664 --> 00:07:11.025
We built the thing that builds the things.

00:07:12.975 --> 00:07:14.039
From nothing.

00:07:14.039 --> 00:07:15.185
To everything.

00:07:16.735 --> 00:07:17.204
Tony.

00:07:17.204 --> 00:07:19.548
If you are watching this.

00:07:19.548 --> 00:07:21.705
It's not janky anymore.

00:07:21.705 --> 00:07:22.455
Press C.
